Z||000042||kevin||10-24-2001||01:28 AM||||I suggest taking them out for somethihng to eat. Nothing fancy, maybe pizza or a inexpensive Italian restaurant. Afterwards, take them to the pre-arrainged Fiero club meeting. There, they will meet all the wonderfull wholesome American Fiero afficianados who can better explain the attributes of owning a car loved by so many. Or, have them e-mail me. I'm close, I'll be happy to speek to them. If I convince them that you indeed "need" a Fiero, then you owe me a pizza dinner. ||||reg||1
